8/15/2007    COMMENTS ON ETG SIMULATIONS WITH GTS
           ------------------------------------------
According to Weixing, the ETG simulations of NSTX require about 10 million
grid points per poloidal plane. In preparation for access to the 250TF
system at NCCS I tried to estimate the amount of memory required to run
that size of a grid. The total number of grid points would be 640 Million
when using 64 toroidal planes. Without the radial domain decomposition, each
MPI process will need to keep the information of a full poloidal plane.
I used GTS on Seaborg to determine how much memory is used.

I didn't the equilibrium and the profiles for NSTX so I used the ones for D3D
and just increased the number of grid points.
I managed to reach 10 million grid points (9982575) per plane by using:
           mpsi=4096
           mthetamax=4

The amount of memory per MPI task varies, of course, with the number of
particles per cell:

         micell       Memory
       ---------     --------
           1          3.14 GB
           2          4.78 GB
           4          7.28 GB estimated

Each dual-core Jaguar node presently has a total of 4 GB so only a run using
micell=1 would be possible and that, by using only a single MPI task per node.
We would need to use OpenMP to keep both cores busy.
The Jaguar upgrade will have 4 cores per node and a total of 8 GB per node.
This would allow an micell=4 job if using a single MPI process per node and
OpenMP to parallelize the work between the 4 cores on that node.

